      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To determine the fraction of the items on the menu that I can eat, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the total number of dishes on the menu:**\n\n   We know that one fifth of the menu is meatless dishes. Since there are 4 meatless dishes, this means that:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{5} \\text{ of the menu} = 4 \\text{ dishes}\n   \\]\n   Therefore, the total number of dishes on the menu is:\n   \\[\n   4 \\text{ dishes} \\times 5 = 20 \\text{ dishes}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Identify the number of dishes I can eat:**\n\n   Out of the 20 dishes, 4 are meatless and 3 of those meatless dishes contain gluten. This means I can eat the 4 meatless dishes that do not contain gluten:\n   \\[\n   4 \\text{ meatless dishes}\n   \\]\n   So, the number of dishes I can eat is 4.\n\n3. **Calculate the fraction of the menu I can eat:**\n\n   The fraction of the dishes on the menu that I can eat is the number of dishes I can eat divided by the total number of dishes:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{\\text{Number of dishes I can eat}}{\\text{Total number of dishes}} = \\frac{4}{20}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Simplify the fraction:**\n\n   To simplify \\(\\frac{4}{20}\\), we divide both the numerator and the denominator by their greatest common divisor, which is 4:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{4 \\div 4}{20 \\div 4} = \\frac{1}{5}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the fraction of the items on the menu that I can eat is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{1}{5}}\\).",
